#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722883 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad988a8-45a6-54b9-8d2d-a5010894e504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722881} {:answer/id #uuid "4c84860f-9f3e-52d2-96c9-51348d15e425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722886} {:answer/id #uuid "7166d653-9122-5bdd-aff6-4c11e561f0ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722888} {:answer/id #uuid "bf2a9fb8-9d35-5bd9-bb62-0cdae22dfad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722898} {:answer/id #uuid "d4086dc1-9d7f-5c5e-9739-550288c5a802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf2a9fb8-9d35-5bd9-bb62-0cdae22dfad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722898} :answer-field/id #uuid "7be6981d-1ef9-59b0-8ae4-46b79a8af131" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34339dac-6623-5614-8f75-d6805028c497" :question/problem "Calculate the outward flux of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(2 x - y)\\,\\mathbf i+(x + 2 y)\\,\\mathbf j$ across the closed curve $C$ given by $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf i+3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\leq t\\leq 2\\pi$." :question/worked-solution "The curve is traversed once counterclockwise. With the outward normal,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=\\oint_C P\\,\\mathrm{d}y-Q\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}(P y\\prime-Q x\\prime)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the components along the supplied curve and differentiate its coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t)&=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y(t)=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\P(x(t),y(t))&=- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\Q(x(t),y(t))&=6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\x\\prime(t)&=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y\\prime(t)=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the flux integrand, keeping the subtraction sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP y\\prime-Q x\\prime&=\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\quad-\\left(6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&=6 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}-8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}+6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t=1$, simplify the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP y\\prime-Q x\\prime&=- 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}+6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor terms containing a remaining factor $\\cos t$, use $u=\\sin t$, $\\mathrm{d}u=\\cos t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nIntegrate these terms separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int - 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=- 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 6\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=6 t+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the definite integral, the constants cancel. Evaluate each contribution at the two endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[- 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=0\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[6 t\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=12 \\pi\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=12 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the contributions gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=(0) + (12 \\pi)=12 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "006c939b-e524-5b51-b66c-7c28cea0694a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 36 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722875} {:answer/id #uuid "56d28e24-93bf-5580-87e3-b069b517d972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722887} {:answer/id #uuid "a3eeabc1-9137-5cc5-9d51-91e091d5b455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722894} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2a8742-1974-5ea9-81ed-efc2c8cfa919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 18 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722908} {:answer/id #uuid "ff49164e-9506-5a03-b9f9-669edc2e9872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 72 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "006c939b-e524-5b51-b66c-7c28cea0694a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 36 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722875} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d2703ad-bb68-5750-8e49-3cd833e3b179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be78fc52-cebc-5baa-bcf1-30bebb2927ac" :question/problem "Calculate the outward flux of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(- 2 x)\\,\\mathbf i+(- 2 x - 2 y)\\,\\mathbf j$ across the closed curve $C$ given by $\\mathbf r(t)=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf i+3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\leq t\\leq 2\\pi$." :question/worked-solution "The curve is traversed once counterclockwise. With the outward normal,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=\\oint_C P\\,\\mathrm{d}y-Q\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}(P y\\prime-Q x\\prime)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the components along the supplied curve and differentiate its coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t)&=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y(t)=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\P(x(t),y(t))&=- 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\Q(x(t),y(t))&=- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\x\\prime(t)&=- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y\\prime(t)=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the flux integrand, keeping the subtraction sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP y\\prime-Q x\\prime&=\\left(- 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\quad-\\left(- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&=- 18 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}-18 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}-18 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t=1$, simplify the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP y\\prime-Q x\\prime&=- 18 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}-18.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor terms containing a remaining factor $\\cos t$, use $u=\\sin t$, $\\mathrm{d}u=\\cos t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nIntegrate these terms separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int - 18 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=- 9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int -18\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=- 18 t+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the definite integral, the constants cancel. Evaluate each contribution at the two endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[- 9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=0\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[- 18 t\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=- 36 \\pi\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=- 36 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the contributions gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=(0) + (- 36 \\pi)=- 36 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71cbc49e-0f33-59d9-81ed-98b72708dd68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722889} {:answer/id #uuid "ae6679a0-173f-59d7-a4e6-f8d4e8568393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722896} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b4eeb5-3a27-5ea3-865d-4a4d54b5dff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722900} {:answer/id #uuid "d5215937-fdc4-5f2c-9c76-2def6561b888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722902} {:answer/id #uuid "e075d528-b030-5019-9026-c9a486e8147d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5215937-fdc4-5f2c-9c76-2def6561b888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722902} :answer-field/id #uuid "798b2b95-b031-5fa4-87e0-7523a05f05e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df52ea00-672b-5c4d-a979-3ac391774a62" :question/problem "Calculate the outward flux of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(x + 2 y)\\,\\mathbf i+(x - y)\\,\\mathbf j$ across the closed curve $C$ given by $\\mathbf r(t)=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf i+3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\leq t\\leq 2\\pi$." :question/worked-solution "The curve is traversed once counterclockwise. With the outward normal,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=\\oint_C P\\,\\mathrm{d}y-Q\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}(P y\\prime-Q x\\prime)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the components along the supplied curve and differentiate its coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t)&=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y(t)=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\P(x(t),y(t))&=6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\Q(x(t),y(t))&=- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\x\\prime(t)&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y\\prime(t)=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the flux integrand, keeping the subtraction sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP y\\prime-Q x\\prime&=\\left(6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\quad-\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&=- 6 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}+22 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}+6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the other powers, use $\\cos^2t=\\frac{1+\\cos(2t)}2$, $\\sin^2t=\\frac{1-\\cos(2t)}2$.\n\nFor terms containing a remaining factor $\\cos t$, use $u=\\sin t$, $\\mathrm{d}u=\\cos t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nIntegrate these terms separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=3 t + \\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 22 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=11 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int - 6 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=- 3 t + \\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the definite integral, the constants cancel. Evaluate each contribution at the two endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[3 t + \\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=6 \\pi\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=6 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[11 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=0\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[- 3 t + \\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=- 6 \\pi\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=- 6 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the contributions gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=(6 \\pi) + (0) + (- 6 \\pi)=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722907 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a9e226-43f9-5f12-bd60-072903292d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 16 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722876} {:answer/id #uuid "1972a294-67a1-5ccd-ab41-2f0104403ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722880} {:answer/id #uuid "a38f09fb-adfd-5303-919b-af30559a3ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722893} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2da741-2ea0-54ea-8dde-5e9bf09cfcf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722895} {:answer/id #uuid "d979f826-b348-5e5d-b83d-afde2d7694fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa2da741-2ea0-54ea-8dde-5e9bf09cfcf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722895} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c19136-9a4b-5ca8-957e-2e1968e09f05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1cc6b27-229d-5fb1-ac00-d4fc9fcaed78" :question/problem "Calculate the outward flux of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(- 2 x - y)\\,\\mathbf i+(2 x + 2 y)\\,\\mathbf j$ across the closed curve $C$ given by $\\mathbf r(t)=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf i+2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\leq t\\leq 2\\pi$." :question/worked-solution "The curve is traversed once counterclockwise. With the outward normal,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=\\oint_C P\\,\\mathrm{d}y-Q\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}(P y\\prime-Q x\\prime)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the components along the supplied curve and differentiate its coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t)&=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y(t)=2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\P(x(t),y(t))&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\Q(x(t),y(t))&=4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\x\\prime(t)&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y\\prime(t)=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the flux integrand, keeping the subtraction sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP y\\prime-Q x\\prime&=\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\quad-\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&=8 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}+4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}-8 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the other powers, use $\\cos^2t=\\frac{1+\\cos(2t)}2$, $\\sin^2t=\\frac{1-\\cos(2t)}2$.\n\nFor terms containing a remaining factor $\\cos t$, use $u=\\sin t$, $\\mathrm{d}u=\\cos t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nIntegrate these terms separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int - 8 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=- 4 t - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 8 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=4 t - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the definite integral, the constants cancel. Evaluate each contribution at the two endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[- 4 t - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=- 8 \\pi\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=- 8 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=0\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[4 t - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=8 \\pi\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=8 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the contributions gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=(- 8 \\pi) + (0) + (8 \\pi)=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "443a604c-7870-59bf-b1c0-1da6c989c2f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722921} {:answer/id #uuid "4aca1596-23f0-5c4b-9da5-9c69eddbdabb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722922} {:answer/id #uuid "4e44dcf9-d1f1-5eae-b5f6-a9c65f056492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722923} {:answer/id #uuid "8f731888-7bdb-54c3-8463-c38c2cf2d5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722930} {:answer/id #uuid "b3be4ae3-6872-567c-a234-b68ee6dbc6cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "443a604c-7870-59bf-b1c0-1da6c989c2f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722921} :answer-field/id #uuid "15fdb7e0-6744-5d3f-9ff0-997c288db6bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "78c47eaf-5815-519d-bfe8-7f7f8e62a547" :question/problem "Calculate the outward flux of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(2 x - y)\\,\\mathbf i+(x - y^{3})\\,\\mathbf j$ across the closed curve $C$ given by $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf i+\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf j$ for $0\\leq t\\leq 2\\pi$." :question/worked-solution "The curve is traversed once counterclockwise. With the outward normal,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=\\oint_C P\\,\\mathrm{d}y-Q\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int_0^{2\\pi}(P y\\prime-Q x\\prime)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the components along the supplied curve and differentiate its coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t)&=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y(t)=\\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\P(x(t),y(t))&=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\Q(x(t),y(t))&=- \\sin^{3}{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\x\\prime(t)&=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad y\\prime(t)=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the flux integrand, keeping the subtraction sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP y\\prime-Q x\\prime&=\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\quad-\\left(- \\sin^{3}{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad\\cdot\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&=- \\sin^{4}{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\&\\quad{}+2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReduce the fourth power by applying the cosine double-angle identity twice:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin^4t&=\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos(2t)}2\\right)^2\\\\&=\\frac14\\left(1-2\\cos(2t)+\\frac{1+\\cos(4t)}2\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3-4\\cos(2t)+\\cos(4t)}8.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the other powers, use $\\cos^2t=\\frac{1+\\cos(2t)}2$.\n\nIntegrate these terms separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=t + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int - \\sin^{4}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t&=- \\frac{3 t}{8} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{4} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}}{32}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the definite integral, the constants cancel. Evaluate each contribution at the two endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[t + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=2 \\pi\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=2 \\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left[- \\frac{3 t}{8} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{4} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}}{32}\\right]_0^{2\\pi}&=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\\\&\\quad-\\left(0\\right)\\\\&=- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the contributions gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Phi&=(2 \\pi) + \\left(- \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{5 \\pi}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c4f565c-3851-5e85-a800-4ab26ea0bee4" :answer/type {:db/id 